[[Open This|artifacts]]

---

In project management, an artifact is a tangible document, template, or output created during a project's lifecycle to help plan, execute, and monitor progress.

These are "living" documents—such as project charters, risk logs, or schedules—that align the team with business goals and are updated to reflect scope changes.